From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: mediatek: tolerate MT6878 HWCCF EPERM

Nothing CMF Phone 1 firmware returns -EPERM for the optional HWCCF infra
request used around the MM_INFRA hardware vote.  The matching MediaTek
vendor driver intentionally ignores the return value and proceeds with the
bounded hardware-voter handshake.

Treat only the observed -EPERM response as non-fatal.  Preserve all other
firmware errors and existing timeout handling for the actual vote.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mtk-pm-domains.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mtk-pm-domains.c b/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mtk-pm-domains.c
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mtk-pm-domains.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mtk-pm-domains.c
@@ -130,6 +130,12 @@ static int scpsys_hwv_infra_request(struct scpsys_domain *pd, bool enable)
 	ret = (long)res.a0;
 	if (ret > 0)
 		ret = -EIO;
+	/* MT6878 vendor firmware denies this optional hint but permits HWV. */
+	if (ret == -EPERM) {
+		dev_warn_once(scpsys->dev,
+			      "optional HWCCF infra request denied; continuing\n");
+		ret = 0;
+	}
 	if (ret) {
 		if (enable)
 			scpsys->infra_req_count--;
-- 
